# PruittHealth Design System

Editorial-healthcare aesthetic for a Microsoft-native compliance/clinical product. Think a premium quarterly report, not a generic SaaS dashboard: refined serif display + humanist sans body, warm-white paper, asymmetric grids, generous negative space, restrained motion. The brand is derived from PruittHealth's tree-and-figure logo (teal + burgundy + sage).

**Source of truth:** `src/app/globals.css` (tokens + `ph-*` utility classes) and `src/app/layout.tsx` (fonts). If anything here conflicts with those files, the files win — and update this rule.

---

## Hard rules (do / don't)

- ✅ Use the `--ph-*` tokens and `ph-*` utility classes — never hardcode hex values in components. In Tailwind use the generated classes: `bg-ph-primary`, `text-ph-burgundy`, `border-ph-gray-200`, etc.
- ✅ Headings (`h1/h2/h3`) render in **Fraunces** automatically (set globally). For display type inside other elements use `font-display`.
- ✅ Body copy = **Public Sans** (`font-sans`, the default). Code/JSON/IDs = **JetBrains Mono** (`font-mono`).
- ✅ Compose classNames with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (clsx + tailwind-merge).
- ✅ Asymmetric layouts (e.g. 5-3-2-2 or 8-4 column splits), `max-w-[1500px]`, page padding `px-10`.
- ❌ **No Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system-ui** for display/body. No generic "AI dashboard" look.
- ❌ **No purple/violet gradients.** No neon. No cold pure-grey backgrounds — the page is warm white (`--ph-gray-50` `#FAFAF8`).
- ❌ Don't invent new accent colors. The palette is teal / burgundy / sage / amber + the warm grays. That's it.
- ❌ Don't put white text on `--sev-minimal`/`--sev-no-harm` without checking contrast (tokens are already AA-tuned; keep them).

