## Typography

- **Display — Fraunces** (variable font, axes `opsz` + `SOFT`). Loaded as `--font-fraunces` → `font-display`. Used automatically on `h1/h2/h3` with `letter-spacing: -0.02em`. Heading optical sizes: h1 `opsz 144`, h2 `opsz 96`, h3 `opsz 48` (all weight 500, `SOFT 50`). In Next.js, Fraunces is configured with `axes` and **no `weight`** (variable). Don't add a `weight` array to it.
- **Body — Public Sans** (`--font-public-sans` → `font-sans`, weights 400/500/600/700). `font-feature-settings: "ss01","ss02"`. This is the default everywhere.
- **Mono — JetBrains Mono** (`--font-jetbrains-mono` → `font-mono`, 400/500). For FHIR/JSON, IDs, F-tags, code chips.
- **KPI number** — class `ph-kpi-num`: Fraunces, 3.5rem, teal, tabular-nums, tight tracking. Use for the big dashboard stats.
- **Eyebrow** — class `ph-eyebrow`: 11px, 600, uppercase, `0.08em` tracking, gray-500. Use above section titles and card headers.

---

## Layout

- Root shell: fixed **260px** sidebar + flexible main (`grid-cols-[260px_1fr]`), with `Header` and a slim `PageFooter`.
- Page content: `max-w-[1500px]`, horizontal padding `px-10`, top padding `pt-6`/`pt-8`.
- **Asymmetric grids on a 12-col base** — e.g. KPI row `5 / 3 / 2 / 2`, body `8 / 4`. Avoid four equal columns; lean into intentional imbalance + negative space.
- Section rhythm: `ph-eyebrow` label → title → content, separated by `ph-rule` dotted dividers in editorial flow.

---

## Components & utility classes (defined in globals.css)

- **`.ph-card`** — white paper, 1px `ph-gray-200` border, 10px radius, `--shadow-card`. The default surface. Add `transition-shadow hover:shadow-[var(--shadow-card-hover)]` for interactive cards.
- **`.ph-card-marquee`** — same card + **4px burgundy left bar** + `--shadow-marquee`. Reserve for the ONE hero/FHIR/"this is the point" card per view.
- **`.ph-rule`** — 1px dotted `ph-gray-200` divider. Use between editorial sections, not as a heavy border.
- **`.ph-grain`** — subtle SVG paper-noise overlay (`::before`, 0.6 opacity, multiply). Apply to hero bands / large empty surfaces for tactile depth, never on dense content.
- **`.ph-eyebrow`**, **`.ph-kpi-num`** — see Typography.
- **`.ph-json-*`** — token colors for the FHIR/JSON tree viewer (key=burgundy, string=teal, number/boolean=amber, null=gray).
- **Severity badge pattern** — pill, per-tier background tint + AA text color from the `--sev-*` scale; Immediate Jeopardy = solid burgundy + white. (See `src/components/dashboard/severity-badge.tsx`.)
- **Decorative `CanopyOrnament`** (`src/components/decorative/canopy.tsx`) — the PruittHealth tree+figure motif as a low-opacity (~6%) background ornament on empty/idle states only. Never at full strength, never over content.
- **Badges/chips** — pill, `ph-primary-soft` bg + `ph-primary` text for neutral; `ph-burgundy-soft` + `ph-burgundy` for accent/synthetic markers; F-tags/codes in `font-mono` on `ph-gray-100`.

---

## Motion (restraint)

- **`.ph-reveal`** — one-time staggered entrance (8px rise + fade, 0.6s ease-out). Apply to cards/rows with incremental `style={{ animationDelay }}` (e.g. `100 + i*60`ms) for a calm cascade on load. This is the primary motion language.
- **`.ph-pulse`** — gentle 2.4s scale/opacity loop for a single "active/processing" indicator (e.g. a live dot). Use sparingly — one per view.
- Prefer `transition-shadow`/`transition-colors` for hover. No bouncy, no parallax, no scroll-jacking. The `motion` (Framer) lib is available for `whileInView` reveals when something should "land" on scroll — keep it subtle.

---

## Icons

- **lucide-react**, thin strokes (`strokeWidth={1.4}`–`1.6`), sized 3–4 (`h-3.5 w-3.5` for inline, `h-10 w-10` for empty-state). Color via `text-ph-*`. No filled/duotone icon sets.

---

## Stack conventions

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript + **Tailwind CSS v4** (CSS-config: tokens live in `globals.css` under `:root` and are exposed to Tailwind via `@theme inline`). There is **no `tailwind.config.js`** — add new tokens in `globals.css` (`:root` + the matching `@theme inline` line), never inline hex.
- shadcn/ui primitives over Radix are available; restyle them to these tokens (don't ship default shadcn slate/zinc).
- `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for class composition. Path alias `@/*` → `src/*`.

---

## When generating new UI, the checklist

1. Surface = `ph-card` (or `ph-card-marquee` for the single hero).
2. Section opens with a `ph-eyebrow` label + Fraunces heading.
3. Colors only from tokens; the one accent is burgundy, used once for emphasis.
4. Asymmetric grid, warm-white page, generous whitespace.
5. Entrance via `ph-reveal` with a small staggered delay; hover via shadow lift.
6. Mono for any code/ID/F-tag; tabular-nums for stat numbers.
7. No Inter/Roboto, no purple gradients, no four-equal-columns, no cold grey.
